            <ArticleTitle>Multilevel lumbar laminotomies for focal spinal stenosis: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of spondylotic lumbar spinal stenosis in an infirm elderly patient successfully treated with multilevel laminotomies. This procedure is less stressful to patients than a full laminectomy. In a selected subgroup of patients with &quot;hourglass&quot; spondylotic stenosis, it may provide adequate decompression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
